  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "For n > 39, is it true that the number of conjugacy classes in the symmetric\ngroup Sn of degree n is never a divisor of the order of Sn ? In other words, is it true\nthat, for n > 39, the number p(n) of integer partitions of n is never a divisor of n!?\n                                                                                  D. MacHale",
